caddy-tui (1.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New [m] screen: manage services. Lists the sites of the Caddyfile and
    edits them (with the wizard form when the block is one it could have
    generated; otherwise only that block in the editor) or removes them.
    Always validated in the context of the whole file, with a backup.
  * Comment lines containing braces no longer confuse the site detection.

 -- Miguel González Oreiro <mgoreiro@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0200

caddy-tui (1.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: caddy-tui --setup-alerts, a guided setup for Telegram alerts: asks
    for the bot token, finds the chat id, and installs a systemd service and
    timer (or a cron job) running caddy-tui --check --quiet --notify.
    --remove-alerts undoes it.
  * New: --notify sends a Telegram message once per problem (again if it
    changes or after 24 hours) and a notice when Caddy recovers.
  * Removed the static example files: the setup replaces them.

 -- Miguel González Oreiro <mgoreiro@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200

caddy-tui (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New headless mode: caddy-tui --check [--quiet] [--json] runs the
    diagnostics once and exits with 0 (ok), 1 (warnings), 2 (problems) or 3
    (could not run), for cron, systemd timers and monitoring.
  * Examples installed: systemd service and timer, Telegram alert script.
  * Diagnostic hints no longer say "offered below" (they are also used
    headless); a fresh Caddy without certificates no longer triggers a warning.

 -- Miguel González Oreiro <mgoreiro@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0200

caddy-tui (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New [h] screen: HTTPS certificates. Lists the certificates Caddy has
    stored (names, issuer, expiry) and warns when one is about to expire, when
    a domain has none yet, or when Let's Encrypt/ACME is failing for it.
  * The diagnostics also report certificate problems.

 -- Miguel González Oreiro <mgoreiro@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200

caddy-tui (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Interface translated: English (default) and Spanish, chosen at startup
    from --lang, CADDY_TUI_LANG, a saved preference ([L] key) or the system
    locale.
  * Packaged as a Debian package (architecture-independent).
  * Fix: snippets such as "(name) {" were counted as sites.

 -- Miguel González Oreiro <mgoreiro@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
